## Purchase Order

1. Find and measure a large hard-sided case.
2. Confirm the internal dimensions and available depth for both side bays.
3. Choose removable caddies that fit the case and the two different HDD sizes.
4. Confirm whether the caddies include SATA-to-USB electronics.
5. Confirm the 3.5-inch drive's 5V and 12V power requirements.
6. Choose a powered USB hub compatible with the two drives.
7. Select a battery power station based on the measured total load and startup requirements.
8. Buy the necessary adapters, cables, mounting hardware, and ventilation parts.
9. Assemble and test the Pi, display, hub, and drives outside the case before cutting or drilling the case.
10. Finalize the mechanical layout, then secure the components and test the complete battery-powered system.

**Build status:** Core computer, display, keyboard, and HDDs are selected or owned. The case, removable bays, USB interfaces, and battery system remain open purchasing decisions until dimensions and electrical compatibility are confirmed.
